tled  rumbling on this page a bunch of  innocent refugees were about to escape  by running towards the high ground but  this idea was quickly ruined after  realizing that titans could climb  mountains and this is visible in the  background of the screenshot  things then transitioned to one of the  most meaningful cuts of the entire  opening involving both air and zeke and  the ocean as we know for years it was  aaron's dream to reach the ocean and  explore the outside because his idea of  freedom was a world where he wasn't  confined inside the walls by titans  however by the time he achieved this  dream he began to understand this wasn't  true freedom as long as there were  enemies across the sea who wanted to  kill them therefore the ocean appearing  in this moment is meant to symbolize  aaron's desire for freedom at any cost  whether that be his new version of  freedom which involves destroying  everything on the other side of the sea  anyway during this scene a shot of zeke  and aaron then briefly appears and this  honestly signifies so many different  things  firstly the dna in the background is a  reference to chapter 137 when zeke  talked about how the nature of life is  to pointlessly multiply without ever  knowing if existence has any meaning  this ties into his core belief that the  eldian race should be euthanized which  is something aaron is obviously against  hence why the two brothers are facing  away from each other instead of towards  each other not only does aaron want the  alien race to continue but he's willing  to sacrifice billions of humans around  the planet just to make sure that can  happen so these two really are complete  opposites  the blood in the background might be  referencing the fact that zeke has royal  blood but at the same time it might also  be alluding to the fact that they are  connected by the blood of their father  after the title appears the opening then  focuses on aaron again as you can see  there are a bunch of birds flying around  him as he walks on top of the wall ever  since the very first chapter there's  always been a subtle connection when it  came to aaron and birds and that's  because burst had the freedom to venture  outside the walls and go to any of the  places they read about in arma's  grandpa's book the survey caused wings  of freedom logo is also the ultimate  confirmation that birds represent  freedom so it makes perfect sense why  there are so many of them around him on  a separate note the idea of eren being  reincarnated as a bird is a theory that  has been jokingly mentioned since the  end of the series but i actually think  aaron would be lucky if that theory  turned out to be true the way i see it  he's either stuck in hell or stuck in  the past dimension making shifters for a  new generation so either way i'd say  being a bird is likely the best option  he could hope for  the opening then gives us a comparison  between how things used to be versus how  they are now with an example being how  it shows marco sasha and the rest of the  104th cadets before flashing forward to  the day of sasha's funeral it does this  again when it shows us berto annie and  rainer only to flash forward to the  present day in mali where reiner is the  only warrior who made it back alive by  this point in the timeline bertolt is  dead and he's imprisoned underground and  ymir who was in this flashback has now  been eaten by poco meanwhile colton the  other warriors watch on as gabby and  falco play together although zeke is  noticeably not there  this moment is followed by shots of levi  and hanji and this is by far the most  depressed the captain has ever looked  during an opening usually if he makes an  appearance it's just him showing off or  looking cool but in this one there's  blood splattered across his face as he  looks up towards the sky a lot of his  frustration in part two comes from the  fact that he still hasn't fulfilled his  promise to kill the beast titan and on  top of that zeke took advantage by  detonating the thunderspear which has  now left the captain weaker than he's  been for a long time  speaking of zeke he then gets his time  to shine and there were a few easter  eggs in this moment it starts off with a  young version of the character playing  catch with sava and it was this game  that led to z becoming such a good  pitcher something that he then used his  advantage as the beast titan the opening  itself directly references this by  transitioning from yangzi throwing a  baseball at sava to adults eat throwing  rocks after inheriting salva's titan  following this there's been a quick shot  of him regenerating which is likely a  throwback to the first episode of part 2  when pretty much his entire body was  rebuilt from scratch thanks to yamir  fritz  one thing worth pointing out about this  whole zeke sequence is that there was a  tree in this shot of him playing catch  there was a different tree in this shot  of him throwing the ball and then there  were even more trees in this shot of him  regenerating this imagery is likely  referring to the tree which contained  the source of all living matter since  that tree was the origin of all these  problems if it wasn't for yamir fritz  falling into this tree then no subjects  of emir would have ever been born so if  you think about it zeke has basically  spent his whole adult life trying to  reverse the impact that this tree had on  the world  as a side note he actually came up with  the idea for the euthanization plan  while playing catch with sarva so it is  fitting that all of these moments were  included in zeke's sequence  anyhow the opening then immediately  switches from zeke to a clip of erin  biting his hand which i guess is another  way of showing that he's ready to fight  against this euthanization ideology  after he bites his hand there's a flash  of white light to indicate his titan  transformation and the next thing we see  is the attack titan about to beat up  reiner in a moment that again references  the first episode of part 2.  the sequence then goes on to show us  moments from all the different warriors  with pique looking absolutely exhausted  her extreme level of tiredness is  because the malian army makes her stay  in the car titan for months at a time  and earlier in the season she'd been in  there for so long that she physically  needed support to stand up as a result  her being exhausted in this screenshot  is pretty appropriate for her character  and is followed by an action shot of the  cart titan with its special cannon  after that we move on to porco as he  stares outside the window and in the  reflection is ymir the connection  between these two characters is unusual  considering that she ate his brother but  then willingly allowed herself to be  taken back to mali so she could be eaten  by him her sacrifice allowed poco to  finally become a warrior after he was  robbed of the title all those years ago  and in one sense you could tell he was  grateful to her for choosing to come  back thanks to amir's memories he was  also able to see what really happened on  the island firsthand which is likely  what he was thinking about while her  reflection was on the window  annie was the next warrior to get some  of the spotlight and surprisingly the  opening shows her outside of the crystal  this was definitely one of the biggest  spoilers in the whole thing however  given that annie being released from her  crystal is a direct consequence of the  rumbling you can understand why they  would want to show it  in this clip she couldn't have been free  for very long since she's still  underground and covered in that titan  fluid so this moment helps to fill in  the gap between the crystal being  destroyed and her confronting hitch  the female titan itself then makes a  brief appearance before switching to  bertolt who is inside his colossal titan  bertolt's appearance coming immediately  after annie was likely done on purpose  due to all those feelings he had for her  and as we know these feelings were  seemingly passed on to armin  in this clip a bloody tear falls down  bertel's sheik which then quite  literally gives life to armin as he  opens his eyes and besides receiving  life the tear possibly also represents  the memories and emotions that he  inherited  a small detail is that the tear came out  of bertolt's right eye specifically  which has happened in at least two  separate visions that armin has seen  throughout the series  the next bit of imagery is the new  colossal titan standing over the  destruction he caused in liberio and the  scene then transitions to inside the  internment zone here we see the  warhammer in the same pose it made  before decapitating the attack titan  only in this opening before aaron's head  gets cut off it switches to him with his  hands around the warhammer crystal  during the episode in which he ate lara  tiber he literally held the crystal in  his hand from start to finish looking  for different ways to break it so i  think this image is symbolizing his  determination to steal this power let's  not forget that he also ate willy tyber  who appeared to be the most obvious  candidate to have the warhammer so  clearly this shifter is something aaron  was on a mission to get  following this we finally move over to  the past dimension and at the beginning  of this sequence the focus is mainly on  the sand this sand is what emirates used  for over 2 000 years to create the  bodies of every pure titan and every  titan shifter and as we saw with zeke it  can also be used to rebuild the flesh of  aldians when in their human form the  camera then pans up to show us the  coordinate which is where the paths  connecting all subjects of emir converge  into one every single branch on the  coordinate represents the bloodlines of  emea's descendants and it's no  coincidence that it looks like a tree  when we consider the origin of our titan  powers  a flashback to her backstory then  flickers on screen as we see the bloody  flower that first appeared in chapter  122.  in that chapter yamir's blood dripped  onto this flower after these elden  soldiers kept shooting her with arrows  and in episode 16 of the final season a  similar flower happened to appear next  to zeke when he was nearly about to die  in both situations when this flower  appeared the characters in question  thought this was going to be the end but  were then miraculously saved by the  power of the titans  in yamir's case the opening shows us her  reaction to being touched by the source  of all living matter hence why she  starts to glow in this moment because  she's acquiring her titan abilities  another flash of light then appears  followed by a glimpse of the clouds and  this is a reference to both aaron and  falco  in chapter 133 falco saw the memory of a  previous beast titan flying above the  clouds and this was his first  realization that his draw titan might be  able to fly as well  at the same time the clouds have  significance to aaron too because the  sights he can see from up there are what  he always thought freedom would look  like that's why the opening shows him  looking over the clouds in amazement  before morphing into a younger version  of the character  a knife then appears next to him and the  reason it shows up at this moment was  pretty brilliant in my opinion  back when the jaeger brothers were  looking inside their father's memories  aaron said to zeke that if someone is  willing to take his freedom then he  wouldn't hesitate to take theirs and at  the time he was talking about how he  used the knife to attack meeks's  kidnappers however in this opening his  words take on a whole new meaning  because he's willing to take the freedom  of everyone outside the island so that  aliens on the island can be free  in between this section there's also  visuals of cannons being fired into the  ocean and this is a nod to how the  global alliance tried to fight back  against the titans swimming towards them  this fleet was meant to be the strongest  weapons humanity had to offer but in the  end they were easily brushed aside like  it was nothing  following that we see a bunch of aliens  in liberia looking up as the rumbling  heads towards them and in the corner you  can see the local town drunk who was  bizarrely already killed in the first  half of the season i'm not exactly sure  why he was resurrected for this opening  but just to be clear this guy never  actually survived to see the rumbling in  action  many of the scouts didn't appear on top  of the walls as silhouettes and from  what i can tell you've got yamir and  historia on the left arm and aaron and  mikasa in the middle the three warriors  on the right and then sasha connie and  jean filling the remaining places  mikasa then throws her scarf over her  shoulder and i probably don't need to  explain that this scarf means everything  to her i mean even till the end she was  still wearing it as it all ties back to  erin being her savior  erin gave her this scarf at a time when  she had no parents and basically nowhere  to live so tamika sir this scarf  symbolizes family it symbolizes home it  gives her strength and in uncertain  times it reminds her that aaron is a  good person  inside the walls of shiganchina they  both race towards a tree with armin  which is a reference to the final volume  cover and also chapter 137  in that chapter armin explained to zeke  that the reason they were born wasn't  just to multiply and that maybe the  purpose of life can be found in these  trivial precious moments like racing  towards that tree on the hill  the three friends are then seen facing  the tree together before mikasa and  armin disappear which is basically a  symbol for how aaron has been alone ever  since that day he kisses storia's hand  armin even explicitly says this in the  final chapter because ever since aaron  saw those fragments of the future he was  put in a position where he had to follow  the path that was laid out for him and  if he had told anyone what he saw then  that would have messed everything up  in the opening he then briefly evolves  into hobo erin and i'll explain why this  version of the character is so  significant  in part one we saw that for a couple of  years after he kissed his story his hand  he still wasn't 100 sure if the future  he saw was guaranteed to happen and for  a while he thought there might be  another way for the people of the island  to survive however hobo aaron is the  first real version of the character who  understood there could be no  alternatives and that the destiny he saw  was inescapable the opening demonstrates  this by zooming into his eye which is  basically their way of showing us what  aaron saw and inside his mind we can see  his founding titan form standing behind  the army of war titans he unleashed  in this shot we have a nice visual of  just how large his founder really is  compared to the titans underneath him  and as i mentioned in my video about all  founding titans the design of his  shifter is based off the source of all  living matter  a steamy aaron then regenerates as he  screams on top of the walls in a moment  that's possibly a throwback to the very  first time he activated the coordinate  his scream in this opening might be  signifying his frustration at having to  follow this path because we know from  the final chapter that he didn't want to  die in the end but he had no choice but  to go along with it since that's what  was destined to happen  on top of that we know the founder was  messing with his perception of reality  as he was experiencing the past present  and future all at the same time so this  scream right here might just be him  going a little bit insane  towards the very climax of the opening a  wall titan steps onto the ground leaving  a bloody footprint behind and this is  definitely a reference to ramsay ramsay  was a young refugee living in mali who  was crushed in chapter 131 and this  footprint is nearly identical to the one  that killed the young refugee  ramsay had more significance to the  story than most rumbling victims as when  aaron saw the future he actually saw a  vision of this kid and then tearfully  apologized to him in the two cross paths  in mali  the scene then cuts to a butterfly  trample by a regular shoe and this part  is meant to emphasize that the world has  always been a cruel place where the  winners survive when the losers die  which is an observation mikasa made a  long long time ago  as a child she witnessed this cruelty on  a much smaller scale but now because of  the rumbling that same cruelty that's  always existed is being dished out to  billions across the globe  now switching over to the lyrics of this  opening there were a couple lines from  the song that i thought were pretty  interesting for example towards the  beginning there was a line that said all  i wanted to do was the right things i  never wanted to be the king and this  perfectly summarizes eren at the  beginning when he thought the entire  world was just the people inside the  walls he wanted to do the right thing by  exterminating the titans and making sure  the sacrifice of all previous scouts  wasn't in vain he never intended to end  up as this all-knowing or powerful being  and given the choice it's highly  doubtful he would have taken it if he  knew what was about to happen if we take  a more literal approach to the lyrics i  never wanted to be the king might also  be a reference to him rejecting carl  fritz's ideology who was the lda king  that established that vow to renounce  war the vow to announce war is directly  opposed to everything aaron has ever  believed because as we know everyone who  was affected by the bow was okay with  the island being destroyed by either the  titans or mali  there was another line that said if i  lose it all outside the wall live to die  another day which is solid confirmation  of the bird reincarnation theory no but  in all seriousness i thought this lyric  was good because aaron is known for the  longest time that he was destined to die  outside the walls in fact he was putting  things in motion to make sure that would  happen so the line left to die another  day could mean this might not be the end  the past dimension has been referred to  by armin and zeke as a world free of  death and like i alluded to earlier the  final panel of the series does imply the  error might be stuck in there just by  himself  anyway people those rule the easter eggs  and references i could find for this  opening and if you liked the video then  i'd appreciate if you dropped a like and  subs if you haven't already  thanks for watching as always and until  the next one  peace out

