iance tried to fight back  against the titans swimming towards them  this fleet was meant to be the strongest  weapons humanity had to offer but in the  end they were easily brushed aside like  it was nothing  following that we see a bunch of aliens  in liberia looking up as the rumbling  heads towards them and in the corner you  can see the local town drunk who was  bizarrely already killed in the first  half of the season i'm not exactly sure  why he was resurrected for this opening  but just to be clear this guy never  actually survived to see the rumbling in  action  many of the scouts didn't appear on top  of the walls as silhouettes and from  what i can tell you've got yamir and  historia on the left arm and aaron and  mikasa in the middle the three warriors  on the right and then sasha connie and  jean filling the remaining places  mikasa then throws her scarf over her  shoulder and i probably don't need to  explain that this scarf means everything  to her i mean even till the end she was  still wearing it as it all ties back to  erin being her savior  erin gave her this scarf at a time when  she had no parents and basically nowhere  to live so tamika sir this scarf  symbolizes family it symbolizes home it  gives her strength and in uncertain  times it reminds her that aaron is a  good person  inside the walls of shiganchina they  both race towards a tree with armin  which is a reference to the final volume  cover and also chapter 137  in that chapter armin explained to zeke  that the reason they were born wasn't  just to multiply and that maybe the  purpose of life can be found in these  trivial precious moments like racing  towards that tree on the hill  the three friends are then seen facing  the tree together before mikasa and  armin disappear which is basically a  symbol for how aaron has been alone ever  since that day he kisses storia's hand  armin even explicitly says this in the  final chapter because ever since aaron  saw those fragments of the future he was  put in a position where he had to follow  the path that was laid out for him and  if he had told anyone what he saw then  that would have messed everything up  in the opening he then briefly evolves  into hobo erin and i'll explain why this  version of the character is so  significant  in part one we saw that for a couple of  years after he kissed his story his hand  he still wasn't 100 sure if the future  he saw was guaranteed to happen and for  a while he thought there might be  another way for the people of the island  to survive however hobo aaron is the  first real version of the character who  understood there could be no  alternatives and that the destiny he saw  was inescapable the opening demonstrates  this by zooming into his eye which is  basically their way of showing us what  aaron saw and inside his mind we can see  his founding titan form standing behind  the army of war titans he unleashed  in this shot we have a nice visual of  just how large his founder really is  compared to the titans underneath him  and as i mentioned in my video about all  founding titans the design of his  shifter is based off the source of all  living matter  a steamy aaron then regenerates as he  screams on top of the walls in a moment  that's possibly a throwback to the very  first time he activated the coordinate  his scream in this opening might be  signifying his frustration at having to  follow this path because we know from  the final chapter that he didn't want to  die in the end but he had no choice but  to go along with it since that's what  was destined to happen  on top of that we know the founder was  messing with his perception of reality  as he was experiencing the past present  and future all at the same time so this  scream right here might just be him  going a little bit insane  towards the very climax of the opening a  wall titan steps onto the ground leaving  a bloody footprint behind and this is  definitely a reference to ramsay ramsay  was a young refugee living in mali who  was crushed in chapter 131 and this  footprint is nearly identical to the one  that killed the young refugee  ramsay had more significance to the  story than most rumbling victims as when  aaron saw the future he actually saw a  vision of this kid and then tearfully  apologized to him in the two cross paths  in mali  the scene then cuts to a butterfly  trample by a regular shoe and this part  is meant to emphasize that the world has  always been a cruel place where the  winners survive when the losers die  which is an observation mikasa made a  long long time ago  as a child she witnessed this cruelty on  a much smaller scale but now because of  the rumbling that same cruelty that's  always existed is being dished out to  billions across the globe  now switching over to the lyrics of this  opening there were a couple lines from  the song that i thought were pretty  interesting for example towards the  beginning there was a line that said all  i wanted to do was the right things i  never wanted to be the king and this  perfectly summarizes eren at the  beginning when he thought the entire  world was just the people inside the  walls he wanted to do the right thing by  exterminating the titans and making sure  the sacrifice of all previous scouts  wasn't in vain he never intended to end  up as this all-knowing or powerful being  and given the choice it's highly  doubtful he would have taken it if he  knew what was about to happen if we take  a more literal approach to the lyrics i  never wanted to be the king might also  be a reference to him rejecting carl  fritz's ideology who was the lda king  that established that vow to renounce  war the vow to announce war is directly  opposed to everything aaron has ever  believed because as we know everyone who  was affected by the bow was okay with  the island being destroyed by either the  titans or mali  there was another line that said if i  lose it all outside the wall live to die  another day which is solid confirmation  of the bird reincarnation theory no but  in all seriousness i thought this lyric  was good because aaron is known for the  longest time that he was destined to die  outside the walls in fact he was putting  things in motion to make sure that would  happen so the line left to die another  day could mean this might not be the end  the past dimension has been referred to  by armin and zeke as a world free of  death and like i alluded to earlier the  final panel of the series does imply the  error might be stuck in there just by  himself  anyway people those rule the easter eggs  and references i could find for this  opening and if you liked the video then  i'd appreciate if you dropped a like and  subs if you haven't already  thanks for watching as always and until  the next one  peace out
 

